  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Governance for Growth - Phase 2, Vanuatu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Governance for Growth program was established in 2006 as a partnership between the Government of Australia and Government of Vanuatu (GoV), with the goal of supporting the GoV to achieve its objectives under the Priorities and Action Agenda 2006-2015 - to create an educated, healthy and wealthy Vanuatu. Its purpose is to generate economic growth and improve service delivery through good governance. The program is a ten-year program divided into two implementation phases. This is the second phase of the program, and the focus will primarily remain unchanged from phase 1. It will support the Vanuatu Government to establish and mature economic and governance reforms in telecommunications, energy, transport, public financial management, tourism and urban development.</narrative>
  </description>
